src/insight/data/actors.json (the bundled threat-group library for threat guides)
also contains data from MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise 20.1 (groups, their descriptions,
campaigns, techniques, software, mitigations and detection strategies), built with
scripts/update_actors.py from the pinned file
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mitre-attack/attack-stix-data/a8db2f52eb933c9c99060c123e088b3326d3a607/enterprise-attack/enterprise-attack-20.1.json
under the same MITRE terms of use. `insight threat-library-sync` downloads the
same release to build a fuller copy on the operator's machine.

This product includes data from the MISP galaxy threat-actor cluster
(https://github.com/MISP/misp-galaxy, clusters/threat-actor.json version 359 at
commit 6d78ff22dd1986ffd1a74bd720e635991a52e91a), dual-licensed under CC0-1.0 or
BSD-2-Clause; Insight uses it under CC0-1.0. src/insight/data/actors.json quotes
its sector labels (cfr-target-category, targeted-sector) and suspected victim
countries (cfr-suspected-victims, from the Council on Foreign Relations Cyber
Operations Tracker as recorded in MISP), each with the MISP entry it came from.

Third-party Python dependencies are installed from requirements.lock and retain
their own licences; scripts/check_licenses.py enforces the permitted set.
